{{!-- A modifier the GM or player adds by hand, priced in SL.

     The Modifier field could only ever take an unlabelled percentage, so anything the system did not know about
     arrived in the breakdown as a bare number. Here the source is recorded with the value and travels out to the
     chat card beside every automatic modifier. Under the 5e Modifiers toggle it also replaces that field outright,
     since 5e has no percentage modifiers at all (p.130-131).

     Added entries are the dialog's own state rather than fields: there is a list of them, and `userEntry` holds one
     value per input name. The two inputs below are deliberately unnamed for the same reason - a named input is a
     field, and every change to one re-renders the dialog. --}}

<div class="form-group manual-modifier-entry" data-tooltip="{{localize 'DIALOG.ManualModifierTT'}}" data-tooltip-direction="LEFT">
  <label>{{localize "DIALOG.ManualModifier"}}</label>
  <div class="form-fields">
    <input type="number" class="manual-modifier-value" placeholder="{{localize 'DIALOG.ManualModifierSL'}}">
    <input type="text" class="manual-modifier-source" placeholder="{{localize 'DIALOG.ManualModifierSource'}}">
    <a data-action="addManualModifier" aria-label="{{localize 'DIALOG.ManualModifierAdd'}}"><i class="fa-solid fa-plus"></i></a>
    {{!-- Inside the fields rather than beside them, so the chips line up under the inputs they came from --}}
    {{#if manualModifiers.length}}
    <div class="manual-modifier-list">
      {{#each manualModifiers}}
      <a class="manual-modifier" data-action="removeManualModifier" data-index="{{this.index}}" data-tooltip="{{localize 'DIALOG.ManualModifierRemove'}}" data-tooltip-direction="LEFT">
        {{this.label}} <i class="fa-solid fa-xmark"></i>
      </a>
      {{/each}}
    </div>
    {{/if}}
  </div>
</div>
